  "caption": "Monday it was Quinn's knee, Wednesday the shoulder, Friday the neck. Quinn made a pain map with pins, and it looked like a crime show.\n\nPain that moves around can be a sign of a more sensitive pain system, which poor sleep, stress and low activity can turn up. Uneven bursts of activity can also shift the load from one area to another.\n\nWhat often helps: steady, gradually increasing exercise, consistent sleep, pacing to avoid boom-and-bust days, and easing stress where you can.\n\nLong morning stiffness, swollen or red joints, fever, weight loss, a rash or pain that keeps worsening are worth a GP check.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
